// The C ABI exports of the test world (decisions 0204, 0207; the zero-C
// audit's B14): like cabi.xo, every top level function here is called
// through its address. The SSA builders build them in test binaries
// only (compiler/ssa build.xo declare_exports), and the test world names
// them itself when it starts (twrun.xo start: rt.fn_addr, atexit.xo and
// the record's TW_KICK; decision 0233). The state is testworld.xo's,
// twrun.xo's and twflags.xo's.
use native/llrt/twflags
use native/llrt/twrun

/// Releases the values the test world keeps, at the end of the test
/// (entry.xo main, through atexit.xo).
fn tw_end() {
  if twflags.on() {
    twrun.end()
  }
}

/// Moves the virtual clock after a deadlock check (pool.xo kick, while
/// the clock is virtual).
fn tw_kick() { twrun.kick() }
